+# StegVerse AI Governance & Continuity Assessment — SYNTHETIC DEMONSTRATION
+
+Issue: https://github.com/StegVerse-Labs/.github/issues/3370
+Template: `docs/GOVERNANCE_ASSESSMENT_SHARE_PACKET.md`
+Status: **SIMULATED — fictional customer, synthetic data. Not an engagement, not a receipt, not revenue.**
+
+Every name, number and system below is invented to show what a finished deliverable looks like. No StegVerse runtime, ledger or Protocol v1.0 receipt was produced or is implied.
+
+---
+
+## 0. Engagement frame (fictional)
+
+| Field | Value |
+|---|---|
+| Customer | "Harbor Lane Bookkeeping" (fictional, 9 staff) |
+| Workflow in scope | AI-assisted vendor-invoice intake → categorization → payment-batch proposal |
+| Out of scope | Payroll, tax filing, bank integrations beyond read-only export |
+| Data handled in this demo | Synthetic invoices only; no customer data |
+| Assessor deliverables | Workflow map, authority/evidence inventory, 5-risk matrix, 30-day plan, review |
+
+## 1. Current-state workflow map
+
+```
+[Vendor email inbox]
+      │ (1) staff forwards PDF
+      ▼
+[AI extraction tool]  ── extracts vendor, amount, due date, GL code guess
+      │ (2) writes row
+      ▼
+[Shared spreadsheet "AP Queue"]
+      │ (3) senior bookkeeper reviews weekly (informal)
+      ▼
+[Payment batch proposal]  ── AI drafts batch from rows marked "OK"
+      │ (4) owner clicks "Approve" in accounting software
+      ▼
+[Bank payment release]  ← consequential, irreversible action
+```
+
+Consequential action: **step 4, payment release.** Every upstream step changes what step 4 does.
+
+## 2. Authority / evidence inventory
+
+| Step | Who may act | Authority recorded? | Evidence before | Evidence after | On DENY / failure |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 Forward | Any staff | No | Email exists | Forwarded copy | Invoice silently missed |
+| 2 Extract | AI tool | No (tool runs on any input) | PDF | Spreadsheet row, no source hash | Wrong amount propagates |
+| 3 Review | Senior bookkeeper | Informal ("OK" cell) | Row | Cell edit, no reviewer identity | Unreviewed rows still eligible |
+| 4 Approve | Owner | Yes (software login) | Batch total only | Software audit log | No pre-release hold on mismatch |
+
+Gap summary: only step 4 has an authenticated actor, and it sees an aggregate, not the per-invoice evidence chain that produced it.
+
+## 3. Five prioritized risks
+
+| # | Risk | Evidence observed (synthetic) | Impact | Likelihood | Remedy | Owner |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Extracted amount differs from source PDF and is paid | 2 of 40 sample rows had transposed digits | High | Medium | Bind each row to the source file's SHA-256 and extracted fields; block batch if re-extraction disagrees | Senior bookkeeper |
+| 2 | Duplicate invoice paid twice (replay) | Same invoice forwarded by two staff → 2 rows | High | Medium | Idempotency key = vendor + invoice no. + amount; reject second occurrence | Senior bookkeeper |
+| 3 | "OK" set by someone without review authority | Cell edits carry no identity | Medium | Medium | Named reviewer list; approval recorded with identity and timestamp | Owner |
+| 4 | Batch approved on stale queue (rows changed after review) | Rows edited after "OK" in sample | High | Low | Freeze queue snapshot at review; approval binds to snapshot hash | Owner |
+| 5 | AI tool outage stops intake with no fallback | No documented manual path | Medium | Low | Written manual-intake procedure; fail closed (hold) rather than auto-approve | Office manager |
+
+Risks 1, 2 and 4 map directly to the conformance negative cases being specified in #3369 (tamper, replay, stale head) — useful for the separately gated pilot conversation, but **this assessment does not require or claim any protocol runtime.**
+
+## 4. Thirty-day plan
+
+| Days | Action | Acceptance check |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1–7 | Inventory: list reviewers, approvers, data sources; add source-file hash column | Every queue row has a hash and named source |
+| 8–14 | Controls: idempotency key, named reviewer field, queue snapshot at review | Duplicate test invoice is rejected; review records identity |
+| 15–21 | Tests: run 10 synthetic invoices incl. tampered amount, duplicate, post-review edit | All three bad cases held, not paid |
+| 22–30 | Review: walk owner through results; decide on fallback procedure | Owner signs acceptance of findings |
+
+## 5. Findings review and handoff
+
+60-minute review covering the map, the five risks and the plan. Written handoff lists each remedy's owner and its acceptance check. Explicit exclusions: no production deployment, penetration test, certification, legal opinion or compliance guarantee.
+
